Thyristors are semiconductor switching devices widely used for controlled rectification, power regulation, motor control, industrial equipment, transportation and high-current applications. While newer technologies such as IGBTs, MOSFETs, silicon carbide and gallium nitride devices are expanding in high-frequency applications, thyristors continue to offer advantages in high-current, surge-intensive and line-frequency systems.

