3 Key Market Drivers
EV Charging and Electrification: Expansion of electric vehicles and charging infrastructure is opening additional opportunities for automotive-grade SCR devices.
Industrial Automation: Motor controls, industrial heaters, welders, rectifiers and static switches continue to support demand for durable thyristor technologies.
Grid and Renewable-Energy Investment: Power conversion and grid-control applications continue to require robust semiconductor switching solutions.

Vertical Industry Watch
Thyristor demand remains closely connected to applications where high current capability, surge tolerance, ruggedness and cost efficiency are critical. Industrial control systems continue to represent an important installed-base opportunity because many motor-control and power-conversion systems operate for extended periods. Electrification is creating new application opportunities, including automotive-grade SCRs for onboard chargers, battery systems and charging stations. At the same time, power-grid modernization and renewable-energy projects are supporting demand for controlled power conversion. Manufacturers are increasingly balancing traditional thyristor strengths against newer semiconductor technologies, creating a market in which application requirements determine technology selection.

